Raise imaplib's 1MB line limit in the MCP email server.

Upstream https://github.com/odysseus-dev/odysseus/issues/2883 fixed this
for the REST path only (routes/email_helpers.py bumps _MAXLINE to 50MB),
which is why the inbox UI works on a large mailbox while the agent's
list_emails fails with "Error: command: UID => got more than 1000000
bytes" -- the MCP server is a separate process and UID SEARCH (UNSEEN)
against a six-figure mailbox returns a response line over imaplib's
default cap. Mirror the same bump here.

--- a/mcp_servers/email_server.py
+++ b/mcp_servers/email_server.py
@@ -9,5 +9,9 @@
 import asyncio
 import imaplib
+# Match routes/email_helpers.py: raise the IMAP line-length limit from the
+# default 1 MB so large mailboxes don't crash with "got more than 1000000
+# bytes" on UID SEARCH. Upstream #2883 fixed only the REST path.
+imaplib._MAXLINE = 50_000_000
 import smtplib
 import email
 import email.header
